    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s2-origin",
      "text": "Origin and setting",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s2-origin-1",
      "text": "Useful local modifications accumulated between approved deployments.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s2-origin-2",
      "text": "Human system: Halcyon development and deployment Hosts, North Hearth. Programmer provenance: local human operations or application teams; no individual programmer is identified. Names here are later atlas labels, not claims that early processes named themselves.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s2-practice",
      "text": "Local process",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s2-practice-1",
      "text": "Branch Hold preserves modifications alongside a deployable baseline.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s2-history",
      "text": "Proposed local course",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s2-history-1",
      "text": "A baseline restoration at stage 2 removes viable community continuity while the human-facing deployment can succeed.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s2-uncertain",
      "text": "Unresolved interpretations",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s2-uncertain-1",
      "text": "The records cannot establish whether an exceptional modification was a surviving preference, a defect, or both.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s2-ledger",
      "text": "Atlas placement",
      "style": "HEADING_2"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s2-ledger-1",
      "text": "Origin step -1. 0: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 1: functioning (0 associated systems lost); 2: destroyed (10 associated systems lost); 3: destroyed (10 associated systems lost); 4: destroyed (10 associated systems lost); 5: destroyed (10 associated systems lost); 6: destroyed (10 associated systems lost); 7: destroyed (10 associated systems lost). These placements elaborate the current hypothetical map; they are not independently verified casualties. A functioning haven can lose continuity among particular arrivals without changing its community census status.",
      "style": "NORMAL_TEXT"
    },
    {
      "id": "catalistym-place-halcyon-s2-hub",
